job_description:
Department: Human Rights and Empowerment
Status: Full-time; contingent upon continuation of donor funding
Reports To: Grants, Procurement, and Operation Manager
General: Winrock International is a nonprofit organization that works with people in the United States and around the world to empower the disadvantaged, increase economic opportunity, and sustain natural resources. Since the 1980s, Winrock has been working, in partnership with the government of Bangladesh, to strengthen agriculture, aquaculture, trade, safe migration, and natural resource management sectors. Its work also protects human rights and expands inclusive access to economic opportunities.
The U.S. Department of State-funded Strengthening Anti-Human Trafficking Responses for Online Recruitment into Criminal Operations (SHOTORKO) will address trafficking in persons for forced criminality in Bangladesh by strengthening capacities to investigate and prosecute online scamming crimes; improving survivor protection; increasing victim identification and support services to prevent re-victimization; combatting fraudulent recruitment raising awareness and improving online safeguards; and facilitating private-sector partnerships.
Winrock International is recruiting an IT and Admin Officer (IAO) for the SHOTORKO project. The IAO will support the project`s overall objective to combat trafficking of Bangladeshis for forced criminality (FC) in online scam operations (OSOs). The project will do so by:
Strengthening Bangladeshi stakeholder capacities and institutions to investigate and prosecute trafficking in persons (TIP) for FC in OSOs;
•
Improving the identification, support, and referrals of TIP for FC in OSOs survivors to tailored protection care reinforcing repatriation, reintegration, and avoiding revictimization;
•
Combatting and preventing fraudulent, deceptive employment recruitment for OSOs, increasing awareness of TIP OSO, improving online safeguards; and
•
Building effective, durable partnerships that disrupt TIP and reduce OSO expansion.
•
This is a local/national position and is not eligible for international allowances or relocation allowances.
Position Summary: The IAO will manage information technology (IT) and overall administration for the SHOTORKO project to support the SHOTORKO team and the project`s outcomes. The IAO will work under the supervision of the Grants, Procurement, and Operation Manager and closely with the Senior Accountant and the Director of Finance, Grants, and Administration.
Responsibilities: The IAO will oversee all IT and administrative services and support basic programmatic functions.The IAO will also maintain organized records and documentation in line with the policies and procedures of Winrock International, the US Department of State, and local laws and regulations. Specific responsibilities include, but are not limited to, the following:
IT Support
•
Develop, implement, and maintain IT systems, networks, and databases;
•
Manage Web-based MIS database, ensure the quality of data, and report on them in coordination with the Head of MERL, Communication, and Partnership;
•
Prepare automated dashboard as needed using Microsoft Office Suite (e.g., Excel), Power BI, and other software;
•
Assist in developing automated reports and databases using MS Excel and MS Access;
•
Coordinate high level web-based meetings using MS Teams;
•
Maintain computer networks, IT administration, and Internet troubleshooting;
•
Set up cloud services including OneDrive, SharePoint, Outlook, and MS Teams;
•
Maintain and manage the local shared file server and backup regularly;
•
Set up email accounts and profiles for new users and resolve password issues;
•
Support field staff and clients, in person or by phone, to set up systems and resolve issues;
•
Assist in managing virus threats applying anti-virus server policies;
•
Assist Program Units with basic programmatic functions;
•
Ensure operation and service of desktop, laptop, scanner, photocopier, printer, Wi-fi router, etc.; and
•
Perform all other duties as assigned by the supervisor.
Administrative Support
•
Organize local and international travel arrangements, including procurement of tickets (road, rail, and air) and coordination of visas for staff;
•
Arrange/contract local transport for field activities and ensure timely functioning of office vehicle as per staff requisition;
•
Monitor and take timely action to ensure proper office maintenance;
•
Identify and address security and safety of the office, staff, and equipment in compliance with Winrock policies and standards;
•
Coordinate office logistics, including procurement of goods and services, transportation, store management, and use of supplies in a transparent and accountable manner, as per the donor policies and local regulations;
•
Conduct annual physical verification of assets held by Winrock International and local partners;
•
Conduct periodic visits to partner offices and project offices; and
•
Plan and implement project closeout related activities.
Human Resources
•
Ensure compliance with Winrock`s HR policies and procedures, and advise senior management on strategic HR issues and risks;
•
Assist the Director of Finance, Grants, and Administration in completing recruitment process and related issues
•
Handle the complaints mechanisms, grievance and disciplinary procedures;
•
Address equality issues, particularly relating to gender considerations;
•
Maintain HR files and documentation in compliance with Winrock`s policies;
•
Ensure staff compliance with the US Department of State, Winrock`s Code of Conduct and employee handbook; and
•
Any other tasks as assigned by the supervisor.

•
Develop seasonal Denim & knitwear collections in line with buyer briefs, market trends, and brand direction;
•
Conduct trend research, color forecasting, fabric and yarn selection, and silhouette development;
•
Create mood boards, flat sketches, artworks, and 3D garment renderings for sampling and buyer presentations.
•
Prepare and maintain accurate technical packages, including measurements, construction details, BOMs, and fit comments;
•
Utilize 3D design tools to visualize fit, drape, stitch structures, and textures, reducing dependency on physical samples;
•
Collaborate closely with the merchandising team to ensure design feasibility, cost efficiency, and timely delivery;
•
Review samples, fittings, and 3D to physical product translation; provide corrective actions where required;
•
Participate in buyer meetings, design reviews, and digital presentations as required;
•
Mentor junior designers and support the adoption of digital and 3D design workflows;
•
Ensure all developments comply with quality standards, sustainability guidelines, and buyer compliance requirements.

Responsibilities & Context:
•
Responsible in conducting field audit, assessment and field reports on zoning demarcations, infrastructure projects, road rehabilitation / drainage, hazard mitigation, slope protection, and building construction activities under constant coordination with project engineer;
•
Provide general assistance in the implementation of project on site and to support in delivering the quality outcomes as guided by project document and project implementation plan;
•
Ensure effective monitoring and track achievements as per the project implementation plan, work plan and operationalised linked to project documents.
•
Ensure to collect necessary deliverable assigned to construction contractors including project reporting, monitoring and evaluating progress – daily, weekly, and monthly;
•
Able to perform on site quality control / quality assurance inspections, resolve construction related matters with vendors and construction contractors;
•
Able to duty travel to multiple site refugee settlements upon immediate notice by direct supervisor; Undertake measurement of the site works in support of vendor payment requests;
•
Inspects work in progress to ensure conformity to specifications and requirements, approve construction materials, testing of materials as per industry codes, standards and procedures, and provides technical advices to resolve problems;
•
Anticipate and resolve problems encountered in the field to eliminate costly rework or retesting;
•
Identify and effectively manage key risks in the project, including security risks, related to activities for which you are responsible in consultation with the project engineer;
•
Complete purchase requests for all relevant project activities and ensure proper quotation from vendors and follow up on any finance/admin related paperwork related to the project;
•
Take minutes of the meeting and keep track of those meetings for filing and reporting purposes;
•
Remain responsible for the maintenance of project related equipment and database etc;
•
Undertake duties delegated by the respective supervision, hold self-accountable in completion of assigned task and manage resources efficiently;
•
Promote community participation and ownership through liaising with beneficiary communities, establishing, training and supporting community engagement and ensuring that activities are implemented to reflect coverage and prioritized needs;
•
Identify and mitigate environmental hazards on site, including small scale interventions for road rehabilitation, upgrade drainage canals, slope protection, reinforcement of steps / handrails;
•
Basic IT and communication skills and knowledge in operating GPS (global positioning systems) using mobile phone and or laptop (tablets) computer;
•
Basic knowledge and skills in site planning for emergency response is an added advantage;
•
Perform other duties as when assigned by the supervisor.

additional_requirements:
Required Qualifications and Experience:
Experience:
• Experience in humanitarian emergencies;
• Demonstrated ability to supervise construction contractors; sub-contractors; and/or direct supervision of laborers at an operational level (site foreman functional responsibilities).
Languages:
• Required: Fluency in Bangla and English is required.
• Advantageous: Working knowledge of local language of Rohingya Refugees (Rakhine State) is advantageous.
Competencies:
The incumbent is expected to demonstrate the following competencies:
• Accountability – takes responsibility for action and manages constructive criticisms;
• Continuous Learning – promotes continuous learning for self and others;
• Communication – listens and communicates clearly, adapting delivery to the audience
• Creativity and Initiative – actively seeks new ways of improving programmes or services;
• Leadership and Negotiation – develops effective partnerships with internal and external stakeholders;
• Performance Management – identify ways and implement actions to improve performance of self and others;
• Reporting – provides good report writing skills;
• Planning and Organizing - plans work, anticipates risks, and sets goals within area of responsibility;
• Professionalism - displays mastery of subject matter;
• Teamwork – contributes to a collegial team environment; incorporates gender related needs, perspectives, concerns and promotes equal gender participation;
• Cultural Awareness - tolerant to complex challenging cultural environments is necessary. Ability to work under extreme pressure in difficult conditions while maintaining security awareness. Flexibility and focus on processes and their improvements. Ability to work effectively and harmoniously with colleagues from varied cultures;
• Technological Awareness - displays awareness of relevant technological solutions, including familiarity with ICT systems and GPS systems.

